-- Version 30 → 31: a project may be readable by all signed-in users (LNL-138).
--
-- One new column and nothing else — a middle read tier between "members only" and
-- "public to the anonymous web". `is_public` already says yes to a caller with no
-- session; this says yes to any account and no to a stranger, so a board can be
-- browsable across the instance without being exposed to the web. It grants
-- reading only: every write gate in AccessControl stays membership-scoped, so a
-- project turned on here is read-only to the signed-in users it newly admits.
--
-- Lands at 30 → 31 rather than 29 → 30 because LNL-134's 29.sqm took the slot
-- first (the versions table and the fix-version rule); this adds one more column
-- on top of that schema, and is independent of it.
--
-- ── The back-fill ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--
-- There is none to do. `ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN` can only supply a constant, and the
-- constant that is correct here is the one the column defaults to: 0, meaning "not
-- visible to all signed-in users". That is exactly the tier every existing project
-- had before this column existed — private projects stay members-only, public ones
-- stay public — so the upgrade changes nothing anybody can see. A project's owner
-- opts in afterwards, per board, from the settings dialog.
--
-- The DEFAULT 0 matches the column as Projects.sq now declares it: a fresh database
-- must end up with the same PRAGMA as a migrated one, and MigrationTest is what
-- enforces that.

ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN visible_to_all_signed_in INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
